Strings
description: five styles, two block qualifiers, and the file-backed forms
- >
  A string picks a **style** — how it is delimited and laid out. The five styles are YAML's, shared by
  the whole family, so the representation lives in the common `yaml/…` namespace; plain is the default
  and carries no marker, and a non-default spelling is preserved through every round-trip. Beyond the
  inline styles, a string may occupy a whole file of its own, or be bytes a format decodes.
- *: plain
- *: single-quoted
- *: double-quoted
- *: literal
- *: folded
- *: own-file
- *: as-binary
